# Article-to-Audio Narration Feature — Implementation Spec v2
### (Corrected against a live Coolify/VPS audit, 12 Sep 2026 — supersedes the earlier draft)

You are implementing a complete feature end-to-end: article text → deep-voice narrated
explainer audio → background/lock-screen playback in a Flutter app → guaranteed cleanup
after listening. Treat the deletion subsystem with the same rigor as you would payment
code — "without fail" is a hard requirement, not a suggestion.

A prior version of this spec assumed things about the VPS that turned out to be false. A
Coolify audit was run and found the real state. **Everything in §0 below is settled
ground truth from that audit — do not re-derive or second-guess it, but DO re-verify
anything time-sensitive (free RAM, port availability) immediately before you deploy,
since numbers may have shifted since the audit.**

---

## 0. Ground truth from the live audit (12 Sep 2026) — do not re-derive

**VPS:** Hostinger KVM2, Coolify `4.0.0-beta.468`. 2 vCPU, **7.8 GB RAM** (not 8 — use
7.8 in all sizing math), **95.8 GB disk / 85.6 GB free** (disk is not a constraint
anywhere in this feature). At audit time: 29% RAM used (~2.3 GB by 15 existing
containers + OS), 5.5 GB free, CPU 8%, load 0.19 — essentially idle.

**What's actually running (nothing about this feature needs to touch these):**
`ainexus` API x2 (Node, port 3000), `ainexus-web` (port 8080, domain monishlabs.com),
`ainexus-litellm` (port 4000 — cloud LLM proxy to Gemini/Groq), `stt-gateway` (host
8090→container 8080), `nas-gateway`, Postgres 16, `redis:7.2` (already in use by
LiteLLM).

**What does NOT exist (contrary to the earlier draft of this spec):**
- **Kokoro is not deployed anywhere.** It exists only as unused code in the `narrator/`
  repo directory (int8 ONNX TTS + a Gemini explainer path) — zero Coolify resource. You
  cannot "extend an existing service" here; you are deploying it for real, for the first
  time.
- **No local LLM exists at all** — no Ollama, no llama.cpp, no Qwen container of any
  kind. This is a genuinely clean slate for §0.1/§1 below.
- **There is no separate "article-summarization-service" container.** News
  summarization goes through the existing `ainexus-litellm` proxy
  (`/api/v1/ai/summarize-articles-batch`, default `news_summarize_provider = litellm`,
  `gemini-direct.js` as the Google transport). **This path is untouched, out of scope,
  hard boundary** — same rule as stated earlier in this project: do not modify, redirect,
  or point anything at this integration. It stays exactly as it is.
- **"Narrator v2" is not a running system to extend.** It's unshipped repo code. This
  build is its actual first deployment — treat it as such, not as two parallel systems.
  There is one system of record here: the services defined in §1 below.

**Flutter app, current reality:**
- Articles currently narrate via **on-device `NativeTtsEngine`** (wrapped by
  `ArticleTtsService`) — not Kokoro, not any server call.
- `just_audio` is present in `pubspec.yaml` but **never imported/used** anywhere.
- **No `audio_service` integration exists.** The only foreground service today is
  `dataSync` (via `flutter_foreground_task`), used for something unrelated to audio —
  **do not touch, repurpose, or replace this FGS.** The new `mediaPlayback` FGS this
  feature needs is an *addition*, running alongside it, not a replacement.

**Constraints this creates:**
- Host ports **8080** (Traefik dashboard + `ainexus-web`) and **8090** (stt-gateway's
  host mapping) are taken. New internal service ports must avoid these numbers even
  though container-internal ports don't strictly need to be globally unique — do it
  anyway to avoid any confusion when reading configs later.
- The existing `redis:7.2` is shared production infrastructure for LiteLLM, running
  `noeviction` eviction policy. **Do not deploy a second Redis container** — reuse this
  one via a dedicated DB index (e.g. DB 1, not DB 0) and a key prefix (e.g.
  `narration:`), and set explicit TTLs on every key this feature writes, so nothing
  accumulates indefinitely on a shared instance that won't evict for you.
- Coolify here is `4.0.0-beta.468`, **not 4.2+**. Deploy triggers are still GET-style on
  this version — do not apply the "4.2 made deploy POST-only" assumption from any prior
  research; verify the actual behavior against this specific version if in doubt.
- The Coolify MCP tool `create_dockerimage_application` (or the equivalent raw API call)
  **does not accept `limits_memory` in the creation call itself** on this Coolify
  version. A memory cap requires a separate follow-up update call. **Apply that cap
  immediately after creation, before the container sees any real load** — an uncapped
  LLM container is exactly how you OOM the other 15 containers already running
  production traffic on this box.

