## 7. Testing

- Structural/correctness: ffprobe duration cap, wpm sanity range, ffmpeg
  silencedetect/astats artifact checks — unchanged from the earlier design.
- **RAM validation (new, given how tight the budget is):** measure `narration-llm`'s
  actual resident memory under a real synthesis job via `docker stats`, confirm it lands
  near the ~3.3 GB estimate (not the un-idle-unloaded ~4 GB+ figure), confirm it actually
  drops back down after `OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE` expires, and confirm the box survives a
  Coolify build/redeploy of another service while a narration job is mid-flight (the
  genuinely tightest moment in the whole design).
- Deletion pipeline test: full cleanup verification, reaper catching missed webhooks,
  retry/backoff/Telegram-alert behavior on simulated failure, idempotent double-delete —
  unchanged from the earlier design.
- Fallback test: force an orchestrator failure/timeout and confirm the Flutter client
  correctly falls back to on-device TTS rather than showing nothing.
- End-to-end on a real device: background playback survives screen lock, auto-advance,
  speed control without pitch artifacts, lock-screen controls, completed icon timing.
- Connectivity test: confirm (or refute) that the VPS can reach huggingface.co before
  relying on Ollama's auto-pull; have the manual-GGUF-via-volume fallback ready either way.

