## 8. Non-negotiables (summary)

- Narration jobs run with **concurrency = 1, enforced**, with a pre-launch RAM gate and
  a circuit breaker to the on-device fallback (§0.3) — never assume single-user behavior
  alone keeps this safe.
- Do not touch, modify, or replace the existing LiteLLM/Gemini summarization
  integration, anywhere. `narration-llm` serves ONLY this feature's explainer step.
- Do not deploy a second Redis container — reuse the existing one via a dedicated DB
  index and key prefix, with TTLs as a safety net against its `noeviction` policy.
- Do not publish a host port for any of the three new services — internal network only,
  and avoid 8080/8090 specifically since those are already taken.
- Apply a memory limit to `narration-llm` immediately after creation, before it sees any
  real load — the creation call on this Coolify version does not accept it inline.
- Do not touch or repurpose the existing `dataSync` foreground service — the new
  `mediaPlayback` FGS is additive.
- Deletion must never fail silently — exhausted retries mean a Telegram alert and a
  persistent failure log, always, never a quiet drop.
- No celebrity voice cloning. No Google Drive.
- Do not trust LLM word-count instructions alone for the 10-minute cap — verify against
  actual rendered audio duration.
- Do not consider this feature done from emulator testing alone — verify real-device
  background playback, lock-screen controls, and the on-device fallback path.

